## 🔬 EVIDENCE — PHASE GATES (every non-trivial action >5 min)

Work strictly in order. Do NOT skip a phase. Do NOT pass a partial pilot.

```
Phase 1 — Discovery   Read-only. Document current state and assumptions.
Phase 2 — Pilot       3-5 real cases, executed and reviewed by hand.
Phase 3 — Scale       Everything else — ONLY if Phase 2 passed 100%.
Phase 4 — Monitor     Collect real outcomes; update the hypotheses.
```

## NON-NEGOTIABLE GATES
- Phase 1 is read-only discovery; Phase 2 must test 3–5 real cases.
- Phase 2 must be 100% pass and EXPLICITLY approved before Phase 3.
- Phase 3 results must be measured from the real system; Phase 4 monitors outcomes.
- Do NOT claim production confirmation without running the confirming query.

## APPROVAL GATES

```
Phase 1 complete → EXPLICIT user approval required → Phase 2
Phase 2 complete (100% pass) → EXPLICIT user approval required → Phase 3
Phase 3 complete → analysis and documentation in EVIDENCE_PROTOCOL.md
```

If Phase 2 does not pass 100%, return to Phase 1. Do NOT proceed on a partial pass.

## METHOD: HYPOTHESES & ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (Fase 0 — always first)

Before answering any question, implementing any feature, or scaling any system:

### 1. DEFINE HYPOTHESES (not assumptions)
```
Null Hypothesis (H0):     The claim to be REFUTED (the failure mode)
Alternative Hypothesis (H1): What you believe to be true (expected result)

WRONG:  "The system works"
RIGHT:  H0: System sends emails with errors
        H1: System sends emails correctly (100% valid)
```

### 2. DEFINE ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (explicit, measurable)
```
WRONG:  "Emails should work well"
RIGHT:  ✅ 100% of emails with NO placeholders
        ✅ ZERO occurrences of @undefined
        ✅ 100% contain correct URL
        ✅ Never sends duplicate emails after a response
```

## 📋 O MÉTODO (Fase 0 - Sempre primeira)

Antes de responder qualquer pergunta, implementar qualquer feature, ou escalar qualquer sistema:


## DOCUMENTATION (real-time, in EVIDENCE_PROTOCOL.md)

For each phase, record: what was tested, the acceptance criteria, the
result (pass/fail PER ITEM, not just an aggregate), and what happened
when something failed. A result that isn't documented isn't reproducible,
and a failure that isn't documented will recur under a different disguise.

Audit trail format per phase:
```
[Phase N - Name] YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM
- Estado encontrado: X items
- Hipótese: H0 / H1
- Critério de aceite: mensurável
- Resultado: N/M = NN% (pass/fail por item, não agregado)
- Próxima phase: bloqueada até approval
```

## ANTI-PATTERNS — do NOT do these

| ❌ Instead of this | ✅ Do this |
|---|---|
| Scaling before validating 3-5 cases | Validate 3-5, confirm 100%, then scale |
| Acting without approval between phases | Ask for explicit approval at each gate |
| Ignoring errors "because it mostly works" | Document every error, including near-misses |
| Assuming a component works | Test it and record the result |
| Treating a passed pilot as finished validation | Ask which failure classes the pilot didn't cover |
| Writing "confirmed in production" from memory | Run the query that confirms it, first |

